// The narrows over a type parameter that CANNOT be answered — each an `E0058` at check time rather
// than a `none`/`false` at run time.
//
// Moving the failure to check time is the point. A narrow answering `none` forever is
// indistinguishable from an honest miss: the program runs, exits 0, and reads back nothing. Every
// shape below used to do exactly that, silently.
//
// Four distinct reasons, one code — a type argument that is well-formed and in scope but cannot serve
// this application, which is what `E0058` means everywhere else too:
//
//   * a COMPOSITE target: the head match tests a parametrized target's reflected type arguments
//     (R3), and a narrow resolves one name — the target's head — so `U` in an argument position has
//     nowhere to be resolved into. (Positions the match *erases* are untouched and stay as
//     permissive as their concrete spellings: `?U`, `(U, int)`, `fn(U)` all test only their head.)
//   * a UNION member: each member's head is tested, so the same limit applies per member.
//   * a NESTED `fn`'s own type parameter: it shadows the enclosing one, and a nested fn is not a
//     forwarding candidate, so no per-call channel reaches it at all.
//   * a `match` ARM's `is U`: the pattern shares the runtime matcher with the expression form but has
//     no operand position to compute a name into (the IR reuses the AST `Pattern` verbatim). Rather
//     than invent a third way to deliver a type argument, the arm points at the expression form —
//     which does resolve, and is what the other cases in this directory pin.
// expect: error E0058 at 32:17
// expect: error E0058 at 36:17
// expect: error E0058 at 41:21
// expect: error E0058 at 48:12
// expect: exit 1
struct User {
    id: int
}

fn composite<U>(v: dyn): ?List<U> {
    return v.as<List<U>>();
}

fn unioned<U>(v: dyn): ?dyn {
    return v.as<U | int>();
}

fn nested<U>(v: dyn): bool {
    fn inner<U>(x: dyn): bool {
        return x is U;
    }
    return inner(v);
}

fn arm<U>(v: dyn): int {
    return match v {
        is U => 1,
        _ => 0,
    };
}
